The horns came with the light. Grimwatch held.

We slept half a day in the Ring, and when I woke, Thorin had already sharpened everything sharpenable, including, somehow, the soup ladle.

Now the true errand begins. The horde is not the sickness — it is the fever. Somewhere under the Ashspur, in the dark galleries our grandmothers sealed, the goblins have raised a war-nest around the old Undergate, and it pours fresh spears onto the road every night.

The galleries are a maze of fallen rock and dead water, and no map of them survives. We will be walking by lantern into country that hates lanterns.

Find the nest. Put a dwarf on its threshold stone. That is all the plan there is, and Muni says all plans longer than that are lies anyway.
